[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5610615994","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122512#issuecomment-5610615994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122512","id":5610615994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTms0ug","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T00:14:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T00:14:50Z","body":"> The one thing I'm unsure about, is if we should have a way to disable this behavior? If a developer artificially increases the resolution (by modifying render_target_size_multiplier) and then later resets it, they probably don't want the swapchain size to be preserved. Do we want to account for that?\r\n\r\nI don't think we should worry too much about it.\r\n\r\nMaybe at some time we want to build in something that if the render resolution is lowered by a significant amount, and has remained unchanged for x amount of time, that we'd want to free up some memory, but most people I know that use render target size multiplier set it once and forget about it.\r\n\r\nA big part of me regrets ever introducing the multiplier, you're just fighting the performance optimisation built into modern runtimes, and most runtimes already have the ability to scale quality up or down on the OS level.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5610615994/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5641328214","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122512#issuecomment-5641328214","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122512","id":5641328214,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUD_WVg","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T22:25:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T22:25:58Z","body":"Needs rebase after #118511's merge","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/